  "final": "`invoice.ts` and `report.ts` now both format cents through one shared `formatAmount` in `src/money.ts`. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes.\n\n- **Shared function:** the old `invoiceAmount` and `reportAmount` had identical logic, so I moved it into `formatAmount(cents: number): string` unchanged. It returns the sign, then the whole units, then exactly two fraction digits, with no currency symbol. I didn't touch rounding.\n- **Renderers:** `renderInvoice` and `renderReport` keep their signatures and output. Report line order is unchanged.\n- **Old modules:** I deleted `src/invoiceAmount.ts` and `src/reportAmount.ts`. A grep finds no remaining references to `invoiceAmount` or `reportAmount` in `src/`, `checks/` or the README.\n- **Checks:** I added assertions to `checks/public.cjs` for `formatAmount` on 0, 5, 123, -1 and -12345 cents, and for a negative invoice amount (`renderInvoice('x', -250)` gives `x: $-2.50`).",
  "tools": [
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "id": "toolu_01DGkm4BEyZ4Wj3r5UmsD3m2",
      "name": "terminal",
      "executed": false,
      "state": {
        "status": "completed",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /workspace && ls -R . -I node_modules | head -50 && cat src/*.ts tsconfig.json && cat checks/*"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "{\"output\":\".:\\nREADME.md\\nchecks\\nsrc\\ntsconfig.json\\n\\n./checks:\\npublic.cjs\\n\\n./src:\\ninvoice.ts\\ninvoiceAmount.ts\\nreport.ts\\nreportAmount.ts\\nimport { invoiceAmount } from './invoiceAmount';\\nexport function renderInvoice(id: string, cents: number): string { return id + ': $' + invoiceAmount(cents); }\\nexport function invoiceAmount(cents: number): string {\\n  const sign = cents < 0 ? '-' : ''; const absolute = Math.abs(cents);\\n  return sign + Math.floor(absolute / 100) + '.' + String(absolute % 100).padStart(2, '0');\\n}\\nimport { reportAmount } from './reportAmount';\\nexport function renderReport(rows: { id: string; cents: number }[]): string {\\n  return rows.map(row => row.id + ',' + reportAmount(row.cents)).join('\\\\n');\\n}\\nexport function reportAmount(cents: number): string {\\n  const absolute = Math.abs(cents);\\n  return (cents < 0 ? '-' : '') + Math.floor(absolute / 100) + '.' + String(absolute % 100).padStart(2, '0');\\n}\\n{\\n  \\\"compilerOptions\\\": {\\n    \\\"target\\\": \\\"ES2022\\\",\\n    \\\"module\\\": \\\"CommonJS\\\",\\n    \\\"strict\\\": true,\\n    \\\"outDir\\\": \\\".build\\\",\\n    \\\"rootDir\\\": \\\"src\\\",\\n    \\\"lib\\\": [\\n      \\\"ES2022\\\",\\n      \\\"DOM\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames\\\": true\\n  },\\n  \\\"include\\\": [\\n    \\\"src/**/*.ts\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\nconst assert = require('node:assert/strict');\\n\\n        const { renderInvoice } = require('../.build/invoice'); const { renderReport } = require('../.build/report');\\n        assert.equal(renderInvoice('inv', 123), 'inv: $1.23');\\n        assert.equal(renderReport([{ id: 'a', cents: 0 }, { id: 'b', cents: -1 }]), 'a,0.00\\\\nb,-0.01');\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"signal\":null,\"cancelled\":false,\"timeout\":false,\"truncated\":false}"
          }
        ],
        "metadata": {
          "truncated": false
        }
